    "body": "So I think the simplest way to fix this and align with contemporary implementations is to simply remove the \"if the valueAsDate attribute applies\" branch from the `valueAsNumber` getter and setter.\n\nThat seems to be what implementations are doing. I'll provide a PR. It's a little strange, but maybe as @tkent-google points out it's fine since only months are stable on a yearly basis. @Hixie also argued that the existing implementations were fine since you wouldn't typically use the controls together.\n",
